**Read:** [Cryogenic Engineering — M. D. Atrey, IIT Bombay](../sources/Cryogenic-Engineering-Atrey.lingua#r_65F71B6VYE8297NF8ZN1D3S783), the complete air-separation sequence; [Guideline for Safe Practices for Cryogenic Air Separation Plants — EIGA 147/22](../sources/Cryogenic-Air-Separation-EIGA.lingua#r_39BST0TM9XV9VEZ14NXVJW7TWA), air preparation and cold-box operation; shared chemical separation methods.

A cryogenic air-separation system coordinates feed purification, refrigeration, distillation and product handling. Coupled columns can exchange condensation and boiling duties across pressure levels. Follow component and enthalpy flows through that coupling; a diagram alone does not establish that the temperature difference or energy balance is feasible.

Stage efficiency, reflux, pressure drop, heat leak, feed condition and product withdrawals affect the result. Major-component separation and trace-contaminant management are connected but distinct calculations. An assumed perfect equilibrium stage is a model of contact, not a measured tray or packing performance.

**Work:** Reconstruct a publicly documented column arrangement from the course. Close the nitrogen/oxygen and enthalpy balances, identify the source of refrigeration and test the condenser/reboiler temperature relation. Change one product's withdrawal and explain its effects on the other streams. State the data needed to turn a stage calculation into a scale and equipment argument.

